BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
[`\frac{2}{-5}`] is [`\frac{2}{5}`] units away from [`0`] on a number line, so [`\abs{\frac{2}{-5}}=\frac{2}{5}\text{.}`] Another way to think about this is that the "positive version" of [`\frac{2}{-5}`] is [`\frac{2}{5}\text{.}`]

